# Local Ollama. Install from https://ollama.com, then `ollama pull llama3.1`.
# Always available with zero configuration below, and always the fallback --
# the app never hard-depends on a paid key.
OLLAMA_URL="http://localhost:11434"
OLLAMA_MODEL="llama3.1"
# Optional. The context window sent with every request (default 16384 tokens: the assistant's prompt and tools
# alone are ~8,800, and a bare `ollama serve` defaults far lower, silently cutting the start of the request), and
# the cap on one reply (default 1024 tokens, so a model that starts repeating itself stops). See ollama.ts.
# OLLAMA_NUM_CTX=16384
# OLLAMA_NUM_PREDICT=1024
# Optional. Whether the model "thinks" before replying. Newer models (qwen3.5, gemma4, bonsai-2) think by default and
# the thinking eats the reply cap above and slows every turn. false/off/0 turns it off, true/on/1 turns it on, or
# low/medium/high sets the effort. Unset sends nothing (what older models like llama3.1 need). See ollama.ts.
# This affects the chat assistant only: JSON side jobs (recipe parsing, calorie estimates, categorizing) never think.
# OLLAMA_THINK=false

# Cloud assistant providers (Stage 2). Both optional -- leave blank and the
# picker simply doesn't offer them. Financial tools and the household's
# learned profile never reach either provider by default, regardless of these
# keys; an admin can opt each provider in separately (password-gated) under
# AdminSettings -> Security -- see assistant/providers/index.ts. A Gemini key
# should only be opted in if its Google Cloud project has billing enabled:
# the free tier lets Google use prompts to improve its products. Paste your own key; this app never
# generates or handles key values for you.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=""
ANTHROPIC_MODEL="claude-sonnet-5"
GEMINI_API_KEY=""
GEMINI_MODEL="gemini-2.5-flash"

# Voice input (Stage 8b), optional. whisper.cpp's whisper-server on this PC turns the microphone's recording into text,
# so the audio never leaves the house. Leave WHISPER_MODEL blank and Settings shows "Whisper isn't set up". Turn it on in
# AdminSettings (assistant.speechBackend = whisper_local); until then POST /api/assistant/transcribe answers 409.
# The server is started on the first recording and stopped again after WHISPER_IDLE_MINUTES of quiet, so the GPU build's
# VRAM is held only while someone is talking to the assistant.
#   WHISPER_MODEL        a ggml model file, e.g. ggml-small.en.bin
#   WHISPER_SERVER_BIN   whisper-server.exe, the CUDA (GPU) build
#   WHISPER_SERVER_BIN_CPU  the CPU build -- the fallback when the GPU build won't start, doesn't really load CUDA, or
#                        fails a request (a game took the VRAM). Either binary alone is enough.
#   WHISPER_DEVICE       gpu (default) or cpu
#   WHISPER_PORT         loopback port for the server (default 8178; give the dev copy a different one, e.g. 8179)
#   WHISPER_THREADS      CPU threads (default 8)
#   WHISPER_IDLE_MINUTES minutes of no recordings before the server is stopped (default 10)
WHISPER_MODEL=""
WHISPER_SERVER_BIN=""
WHISPER_SERVER_BIN_CPU=""
# WHISPER_DEVICE=gpu
# WHISPER_PORT=8178
# WHISPER_THREADS=8
# WHISPER_IDLE_MINUTES=10

PORT=3200

# Overrides where the SQLite file lives (Stage 0.5.1). Leave unset for the real
# database at data/household.db. Set to data/dev.db (via `npx tsx
# scripts/seed-dev-db.ts` then `DB_PATH=data/dev.db npm run dev`) to develop or
# test against fake data instead of the real household database.
DB_PATH=""

# Plaid bank sync for the budget section. Get sandbox keys from
# https://dashboard.plaid.com/ -> Developers -> Keys. Leave blank and the Budget
# section still works for manual entry and statement import -- Plaid just won't
# offer to link real bank accounts. Can also be set from Budget > Settings once
# the app is running, which persists them to the database instead.
PLAID_CLIENT_ID=""
PLAID_SECRET=""
PLAID_ENV="sandbox"

# Kroger: send a grocery list to the household's Kroger cart (kroger.ts). Register an app at
# https://developer.kroger.com (Production environment; Cart, Product and Location APIs, Public)
# and paste its client ID and secret here. The redirect URI must match one registered on that
# app character for character: https://your-domain.example/api/grocery/kroger/callback on the live app,
# http://localhost:3210/api/grocery/kroger/callback on the dev copy. An admin then connects the
# household's Kroger account from Settings, in a browser opened at that same address. Leave all
# three blank and the app simply doesn't offer Kroger.
KROGER_CLIENT_ID=""
KROGER_CLIENT_SECRET=""
KROGER_REDIRECT_URI=""

# Encrypts Plaid access tokens at rest in bank_connections (Stage 0.0.5), the
# Plaid client secret saved from Budget settings, and the Kroger sign-in. A random 32-byte key,
# hex-encoded (64 hex chars). Generate one with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# Losing this key makes existing bank connections undecryptable -- they'd need
# to be re-linked through Plaid. Never commit the real value. To change it,
# don't just edit this line: run scripts/rotate-encryption-key.ts, which
# re-encrypts every stored value with the new key (see SHIP_CHECKLIST.md).
DB_ENCRYPTION_KEY=""

# Signs the express-session cookie (Stage: always-on). Leave blank and the app
# generates one on first boot and remembers it in the database (app_config) --
# set it here instead if you'd rather it not ride along inside every database
# backup file. Generate one the same way as DB_ENCRYPTION_KEY above. Rotating
# this logs every signed-in device out.
SESSION_SECRET=""

# Optional second copy of each daily database snapshot, made outside the
# backupIfNeeded() flow in db.ts -- written to a path OUTSIDE this drive (e.g.
# a second disk or cloud-synced folder) so a lost/damaged disk doesn't also take
# the backups with it. Leave blank to skip. Example: "C:\Users\you\HouseholdBackups"
OFFSITE_BACKUP_DIR=""

# Nutrition: barcode lookups (nutrition/lookup.ts, shared by the food diary's scanner and Pantry).
# Open Food Facts needs no key. USDA FoodData Central is a free key
# (https://fdc.nal.usda.gov/api-key-signup); leave blank and the USDA step is simply skipped.
# `npm run import:usda` (the generic-foods catalogue) needs it too. Paste your own key.
FDC_API_KEY=""
# Optional: how this app identifies itself to Open Food Facts (they ask for a contact).
OFF_USER_AGENT=""
